***************************************************************** 1725 1451   62
CL35,37 Resonance Parameter Evaluation Update, January, 2007.     1725 1451   63
R. O. Sayer, K. H. Guber, L. C. Leal, N. M. Larson (ORNL)         1725 1451   64
                                                                  1725 1451   65
The updated ENDF format now permits the full generality of the    1725 1451   66
Reich-Moore theory, including charged particle exit channels.     1725 1451   67
Consequently, we have updated the ENDF evaluations by adding      1725 1451   68
resonance parameters (RPs) to File 2, MT=151, and by including    1725 1451   69
the corresponding RP covariance matrices in File 32, MT=151.      1725 1451   70
The Reich-Moore format with LRF=3 and LCOMP=1 was                 1725 1451   71
utilized for CL37.  The Reich-Moore Limited (LRF=7, LCOMP=2)      1725 1451   72
format was used for CL35 because the proton exit channel is open  1725 1451   73
(Q = +0.61522 MeV).  The applicable energy range is  0.00001 eV   1725 1451   74
to 1.2 MeV.  Above 1.2 MeV, cross sections from the February 2000 1725 1451   75
ENDF evaluation are used.                                         1725 1451   76
                                                                  1725 1451   77
The Cl evaluations [1,2] were based on fits of many data sets with1725 1451   78
the SAMMY code [3].  In ref [2] we give detailed discussions of   1725 1451   79
the analysis methods used to determine parameter values and       1725 1451   80
uncertainties.  For capture and neutron width uncertainties, for  1725 1451   81
example, for each resonance several SAMMY calculations with       1725 1451   82
different width values were overlaid with the data.  Both the     1725 1451   83
overlay plots and chi-squared changes with width variation were   1725 1451   84
used to determine final uncertainties that were, in most cases,   1725 1451   85
significantly larger than the SAMMY values.  The RADCOP code [4]  1725 1451   86
was used to generate both File 2 and File 32.                     1725 1451   87
                                                                  1725 1451   88
At the time of the Cl evaluation, SAMMY did not incorporate the   1725 1451   89
now available "Prior Uncertainty Parameter", or PUP procedure.    1725 1451   90
Thus, some normalization and background uncertainties were not    1725 1451   91
propagated properly through the sequential analysis of multiple   1725 1451   92
data sets.  Although uncertainties in resonance energies          1725 1451   93
and widths are felt to be realistic, the uncertainties in         1725 1451   94
computed cross sections in valleys between resonances were        1725 1451   95
underestimated.  Furthermore, since File 32 is limited by the     1725 1451   96
current ENDF format to RP uncertainties and correlations,         1725 1451   97
uncertainties in nuclear radii cannot be treated directly.        1725 1451   98
These "normalization/background/radius" effects were represented  1725 1451   99
approximately by adjusting the File 32 uncertainties for the      1725 1451  100
external RPs and for selected resonances in the energy range of   1725 1451  101
the evaluation.                                                   1725 1451  102
                                                                  1725 1451  103
Since the resonance parameter representation does not include the 1725 1451  104
direct capture (DC) part of the capture cross section, the DC     1725 1451  105
component was included as  a "background" 1/v cross section in    1725 1451  106
File 3, sections 1 and 102.   At E = 0.0253 eV, the CL35 (CL37) DC1725 1451  107
cross section is 0.16 (0.31) b, which is a small (large) fraction 1725 1451  108
of the overall capture cross section of 43.60 (0.433) b.          1725 1451  109
The upper energy limit for the DC cross section is estimated [2]  1725 1451  110
to be 10 (100) keV for CL35 (CL37).  The 1/v cross section was    1725 1451  111
extended to 1.0 MeV to ensure continuity in the evaluation range. 1725 1451  112
                                                                  1725 1451  113
