The new ORELA measurements and the older KFK measurements enabled 1725 1451  247
us to extend the resonance parameter representation to 1.2 MeV;   1725 1451  248
the ENDF/B-VI representation above 226 keV, based on calculations 1725 1451  249
utilizing Hauser-Feshbach statistical theory, is inadequate.      1725 1451  250
                                                                  1725 1451  251
SUMMARY AND CONCLUSIONS                                           1725 1451  252
-----------------------                                           1725 1451  253
The Cl data used in this evaluation include recent ORELA          1725 1451  254
high-resolution capture and transmission measurements as well as  1725 1451  255
several older data sets. Since the 35Cl(n,p)35S reaction yields   1725 1451  256
a significant contribution to the total cross section from        1725 1451  257
thermal energies up to about 10 keV, the 35Cl(n,p) data of        1725 1451  258
Koehler [11] and Druyts, et al. [12] were fit to obtain proton    1725 1451  259
width values for several resonances. The proton widths are        1725 1451  260
significant fractions of the total widths for resonances at 398   1725 1451  261
and 4251 eV. When uncertainties are considered, there is good     1725 1451  262
agreement between our resonance parameter calculations and        1725 1451  263
experiment for natCl total cross sections up to 1200 keV, for     1725 1451  264
35Cl(n,p) cross sections up to 100 keV, and for natCl capture     1725 1451  265
cross sections up to 500 keV. Our thermal elastic, capture,       1725 1451  266
(n,p), and total cross sections are in good agreement with the    1725 1451  267
corresponding ENDF/B-VI quantities, which are based primarily on  1725 1451  268
the compilation of Mughabghab [15].                               1725 1451  269
                                                                  1725 1451  270
Our evaluation fits the data much better than does ENDF/B-VI.     1725 1451  271
This new representation should be particularly applicable to      1725 1451  272
improvement of the reliability of criticality safety              1725 1451  273
calculations for systems where Cl is present.                     1725 1451  274
                                                                  1725 1451  275
The present ENDF format does not allow for a resonance parameter  1725 1451  276
representation of charged particle cross sections. A proposal is  1725 1451  277
in preparation for a new ENDF format which will permit the full   1725 1451  278
generality of the Reich-Moore theory, including charged particle  1725 1451  279
penetrabilities.   The parametric representation (File 2) will be 1725 1451  280
made available when the new ENDF format is approved.              1725 1451  281
                                                                  1725 1451  282
